      <div class="compare-card__label">Better spending logic</div>
      <ul>
        <li>Treat college fees as roughly 10% of your total education budget as a starting heuristic — not a fixed rule, but a useful check against overspending.</li>
        <li>Keep the remaining budget for tools, a laptop, online courses, projects, and the math or logic bridge you actually need.</li>
        <li>Spend materially more only when the specific institution has verified placement outcomes, strong faculty, or lab access you cannot get elsewhere.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="compare-card compare-card--gold">
      <div class="compare-card__label">The trap to avoid</div>
      <ul>
        <li>Paying a premium fee just to escape the discomfort of leaving the medical identity behind.</li>
        <li>Choosing the most "impressive-sounding" course name over the one with real hiring data behind it.</li>
        <li>Skipping the proof-of-work step because the degree "should" be enough on its own.</li>
